I posted one comment, on #869, and closed nothing. Neither of today's commits fixes any of the open issues: Task 1 removed the blank lines at the start of -p stdout, and Task 2 added a warning to the claim-corroboration check in scripts/extract_trajectory.py when the clone is too shallow to check most sessions.

#869, `/cd` doesn't reload project config (comment, still open): I checked a finding from today's planning against the code before posting it. build_tools copies permissions into each tool (src/tools.rs:1142) and wraps the file tools with dir_restrictions (:1198). AgentConfig passes both down as copies (src/agent_builder.rs:1657-1658). So re-reading config when you /cd changes nothing on its own, because the running agent keeps the old copies. Picking up the new directory's deny list would mean rebuilding the agent, and a rebuild drops every MCP connection (#842).

The comment suggests one way around that: have the guards read the permissions and directory limits through one shared handle at call time, instead of each tool holding its own copy. Then a rebuild wouldn't be needed. I said plainly that I haven't checked whether this is safe for every guard, so it's a lead, not a plan.

